---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.ts';
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data: no accounts, everything stored on your own device, and how advertising cookies work.`}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <div class="wrap reading">
    <article class="reading-main">
      <header class="reading-head">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </header>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>{SITE.name} is built to need as little of your information as possible. There are no accounts and nothing to sign up for.</p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>Nothing that identifies you. {SITE.name} does not ask for your name, email or any personal details, and it has no login.</p>

        <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
        <p>A few things are saved in your browser's own storage so the site is more useful on your next visit:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your recent calculator history,</li>
          <li>your quiz progress and best scores,</li>
          <li>your best scores in the games.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This stays on your device. It is never sent to us or to anyone else, and clearing your browser data removes it.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE.name} sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics scripts. However, the site is funded by advertising
          through Google AdSense, and Google and its partners may use cookies to serve ads.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this
          site and other sites on the internet. Google may use the DART cookie (a DoubleClick cookie) for this purpose.
          You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting{' '}
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads">Google's Ads Settings</a>. Alternatively, you can opt out of
          third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting{' '}
          <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also control cookies through your browser settings: most browsers let you block or delete cookies, though
          blocking them may affect how some sites work. Clearing your browser data also removes the calculator history,
          quiz progress and game scores described above.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>Some pages link to other websites. Once you follow a link, that site's own privacy policy applies. We do not control those sites.</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>The site is safe for students to use. Because it collects no personal information and needs no account, there is nothing for a child to share.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top will be updated.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about privacy? Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
